{"title":"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b109bbad8ddff023f591be8a7ed806fdcc5938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 7, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is an arithmetic sequence with three terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three of the five numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb0b8d2ef8cc9c26435662d4f1d52bc6f5ee1aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5, 10, 13, 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> can be chosen to form an arithmetic sequence with three terms. What are the three numbers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that the only numbers that give an arithmetic sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3a11f44747270375eda17d30b2100c5a524893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{5, 10, 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"29\" />. Using any of the other three terms results in a sequence that is not arithmetic.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 21/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 552/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.664      1 2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    6.664      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37297:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060313 and revision id 287956. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}